<newsitem itemid="202210" id="root" date="1996-11-20" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Tongaat-Hulett interim shr, div rise.</title>
<headline>Tongaat-Hulett interim shr, div rise.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Sept 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Headline shr (cts)    200	   vs  150.6</p>
<p>    Total shr (cts)	 213.7	 vs  150.6</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 52.0	  vs   40.0</p>
<p>    Net earnings	    201.6	 vs  138.7</p>
<p>    Headline earnings     188.7	 vs  138.7</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   289.5	 vs  201.6</p>
<p>    Tax			 91.6	  vs  73.3</p>
<p>    Interest received     42.4	  vs  2.9 paid</p>
<p>    Turnover		  2,326.9     vs  2,238.6</p>
<p>Div payable January 15</p>
<p>on register December 6</p>
<p>Full name: Tongaat-Hulett Group Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts polled by Reuters forecast earnings for the half year ended September 30 between 176.2 and 185.0 cents per share, with consensus at 179.7 cents. The dividend was forecast between 46.8 and 49.0 with consensus at 47.6 cents.</p>
<p>Industrial and food group Tongaat-Hulett said that it had resolved to award capitalisation shares to shareholders on the register at December 6 in the ratio that 56 cents bears to the weighted average of traded price of the company's shares on the bourse during the three day period ending January 9 for every share held.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
